{"id": "unknown-2026-06-13-002", "date": "2026-06-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["concerns"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Supply chain concerns cloud India’s holiday season export outlook", "content": "As holiday-season shipments get underway, Indian apparel and home textile exporters are navigating choppy waters. \nThe West Asia crisis has reportedly disrupted key trade routes and driven up freight costs, while longer payment cycles are tying up more working capital. \nExporters hope easing geopolitical tensions will help restore logistics stability. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/supply-chain-concerns-cloud-india-s-holiday-season-export-outlook-310960-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-13-003", "date": "2026-06-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s Odisha to set up textile cluster on defunct spinning mill site", "content": "India’s Odisha state has decided to set up a modern textile industry cluster in the premises of Shree Sarala Weavers Cooperative Spinning Mill at Tirtol in Jagatsinghpur district. \nThe mill has been closed since 1999. \nAs a first step, Odisha Industrial Infrastructure Development Corporation has given $2.41 million to the handloom and knitting industries department to get possession of the mill property. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-odisha-to-set-up-textile-cluster-on-defunct-spinning-mill-site-310959-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-13-004", "date": "2026-06-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Indian textile industry poised to hit $350 bn by 2030: Minister", "content": "India’s domestic textile market has grown from about $63 billion in FY15 to over $168.2 billion now, reflecting robust expansion and increasing contribution to the economy, according to Minister of Textiles Giriraj Singh.\nThe country’s textile industry has expanded to nearly $190 billion in FY26 and is poised to hit $350 billion by 2030.\nIndia has emerged as a major force in technical textiles as well.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/indian-textile-industry-poised-to-hit-350-bn-by-2030-minister-310966-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
